cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this note, please cite it as below."
title: "An N^sqrt(2)+o(1) upper bound for Hurwitz's sum-of-squares problem from the ETH-refutation construction"
authors:
  - family-names: Siemaszko
    given-names: Jacob
date-released: 2026-11-07
version: "0.2"
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24024947
repository-code: "https://github.com/JacobSiemaszko/White-papers"
abstract: >-
  Theorem B of "A 2^{o(n)} Time Algorithm for 3-SAT" (Claude/Anthropic, Oct 2026)
  decomposes the crossing [x=v][y=u] into pieces of low row- and column-rank.
  Counting the rank-1 terms of that decomposition in the cheaper direction gives
  P(N) <= N^{sqrt(2)+o(1)} for Naslund's crossing-width P(N), hence
  B_Q(SOS_N) <= N^{sqrt(2)+o(1)} and sigma_C(N) <= N^{sqrt(2)+o(1)}, improving the
  exponent 1.615 of Hrubes (CCC 2024). Research note, not peer-reviewed; depends
  on the correctness of Theorem B.
